{"name":"Syrah Soil","hex":"#a16717","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"syrah","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark-skinned variety of grape, used to produce red wines.","A wine produced from this variety of grape."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/syrah"},{"term":"soil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixture of mineral particles and organic material, used to support plant growth.","The unconsolidated mineral or organic material on the immediate surface of the earth that serves as a natural medium for the growth of land plants."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make dirty.","To become dirty or soiled."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Syrah","blocks":[{"text":"Syrah, also known as Shiraz, is a dark-skinned grape variety grown throughout the world and used primarily to produce red wine. In 1999, Syrah was found to be the offspring of two obscure grapes from southeastern France, Dureza and Mondeuse Blanche. Syrah should not be confused with Petite Sirah, a cross of Syrah with Peloursin dating from 1880."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Syrah.jpg/330px-Syrah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syrah","wikidata":"Q332720"},{"title":"Soil","blocks":[{"text":"Soil, also commonly referred to as earth, is a mixture of organic matter, minerals, gases, water, and organisms that together support the life of plants and soil organisms. Some scientific definitions distinguish dirt from soil by restricting the former term specifically to displaced soil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Stagnogley.JPG/330px-Stagnogley.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soil","wikidata":"Q36133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/89/Rhones_Alpes_region_with_Ardeche%2C_Drome%2C_Isere_and_Savoie_highlighted.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/89/Rhones_Alpes_region_with_Ardeche%2C_Drome%2C_Isere_and_Savoie_highlighted.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The Rhône-Alpes region. Dureza is believed to have originated in the Ardèche (#1) in the southwest and moved east/northeast into Drôme (#2) and Isère (#3). Somewhere in this area, most likely in Isère, the vine crossed with Mondeuse blanche, a variety native to the Savoie region (#4), to produce Syrah.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARhones_Alpes_region_with_Ardeche%2C_Drome%2C_Isere_and_Savoie_highlighted.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Shiraz_Grapes.jpg/500px-Shiraz_Grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Shiraz_Grapes.jpg/1280px-Shiraz_Grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Shiraz_Grapes.jpg/500px-Shiraz_Grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clusters of Syrah grapes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShiraz_Grapes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Syrah_leaf.JPG/500px-Syrah_leaf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Syrah_leaf.JPG/500px-Syrah_leaf.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Syrah leaf","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASyrah_leaf.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Boushey_Syrah.JPG/500px-Boushey_Syrah.JPG?utm_so